 ### [Parallel Image Compositing with Overlapping](3554-parallel-image-compositing-with-overlapping.md)
-A distributed strategy where ray segments are transmitted to their responsible processors immediately upon generation, rather than waiting for local ray-casting to complete. It sets itself apart from non-overlapping methods by overlapping communication with computation, which reduces network congestion and improves overall image compositing performance by up to 40%. Choose this when network bandwidth can handle frequent, smaller messages and when load balancing across processors is critical.
