 ### [Ray Compaction](4039-ray-compaction.md)
-A parallel primitive that filters a list of active rays by removing terminated ones and compacting the survivors into a dense, contiguous buffer. It sets itself apart from [Ray Buffer Reordering](4073-ray-buffer-reordering.md) by serving as a foundational atomic-indexing step, whereas [In-Kernel Stream Compaction (InK-Compact)](6991-in-kernel-stream-compaction-ink-compact.md) avoids separate prefix-sum launches [G]. Choose this when ray termination rates are high and memory locality for active rays is required.
